  "id": "COMPOUND:25754 - PROTEIN:1026",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex but consistent relationship between the compound [(3S,8R,10R)-8-hydroxy-3-methyl-5-oxo-2,9-dioxatricyclo[4.3.1.03,8]decan-10-yl]methyl benzoate and Cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitor 1 (CDKI1). This compound is identified as a target of multiple entities, including Potassium channel subfamily K member 9, which in turn is a target of several other compounds. These include 7,8-Dimethoxy-9,10-dihydrophenanthrene-2,4,6-triol and Cyclohexanol, 2-methylene-5-(1-methylethenyl)-, (1S-cis)-, all of which are ultimately linked to CDKI1. The evidence suggests that the compound may act through a pathway involving potassium channel activity, which could influence cellular processes that are modulated by CDKI1. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential role of potassium channels in the regulation of CDKI1, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
